                "border": "none",
                "display": "block",
                "position": "static",
                "top": "auto",
                "left": "auto",
                "right": "auto",
                "bottom": "auto",
                "zIndex": 1
              },
              "text": "The most effective way to change your habits is to focus not on what you want to achieve, but on who you wish to become. Your outcomes are a lagging measure of your habits. Your net worth is a lagging measure of your financial habits. Your weight is a lagging measure of your eating habits. Your knowledge is a lagging measure of your reading habits. You get what you repeat. "
